diff --git a/docs/api/sections/webhooks.md b/docs/api/sections/webhooks.md
index a4f48b5..7fefc0e 100644
--- a/docs/api/sections/webhooks.md
+++ b/docs/api/sections/webhooks.md
@@ -2,6 +2,14 @@
 
 Webhooks notify another application when something happens on a board. Only account admins can list, view, create, update, delete, or reactivate webhooks.
 
+## Receiving events
+
+After a board event commits, Fizzy sends a POST to each active webhook subscribed to its action. The default body is JSON with the event's `id`, `action`, `created_at`, `board`, `creator`, and `eventable` (card or comment). Recognized Slack, Campfire, and Basecamp chat URLs receive a message and link instead. Destinations must resolve to a public IP address; redirects aren't followed.
+
+To verify a request, compare `X-Webhook-Signature` with the hex-encoded HMAC-SHA256 of the **raw request body** using the webhook's signing secret. Each delivery has a stable `Idempotency-Key` (its log ID). Fizzy makes at most one POST attempt per webhook/event pair and doesn't resend on a timeout or an ambiguous outcome. A receiver that needs exactly-once processing should record the key transactionally with its work: HTTP alone can't confirm whether a receiver processed a request after the connection was lost.
+
+A 2xx response is a success. Other HTTP responses and connection failures count toward deactivation. A webhook is switched off when a run of at least ten consecutive failures spans at least one hour. A success or a manual reactivation resets the streak. Delivery history is kept for one week.
+
 ## `GET /:account_slug/boards/:board_id/webhooks`
 
 Returns a paginated list of webhooks for a board.
